---
import Glyph from './Glyph.astro';
import InstallBadge from './InstallBadge.astro';
import HeadsetModel from './HeadsetModel.astro';
import { DOWNLOADS, RELEASES, blob, downloadUrl, url } from '../data/site';

// how to start it the first time, per system (the install tutorial's words)
const FIRST: Record<string, string> = {
  windows: 'open FramePort.exe. At “Windows protected your PC” choose More info → Run anyway (the app is signed with a free certificate).',
  macos: 'right-click FramePort.app → Open → Open (macOS asks once for apps from outside the App Store).',
  linux: 'run FramePort/FramePort from the unpacked folder.',
  'linux-arm64': 'run FramePort/FramePort from the unpacked folder.',
};
const pageUrl = new URL(url('install/'), Astro.site).href;
const badgeUrl = new URL(url('media/install-with-frameport.svg'), Astro.site).href;
const snippet = `<a href="${pageUrl}?manifest=https%3A%2F%2Fexample.com%2Fmy-game.json">
  <img src="${badgeUrl}"
       alt="Install with FramePort" width="216" height="60">
</a>`;
---
<section class="section" id="install">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head reveal">
      <p class="label"><b>05</b> Install</p>
      <h2>Three steps. The first two only once.</h2>
    </div>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step reveal">
        <span class="num pc">1</span>
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Download FramePort</h3>
          <p>Unzip it and start FramePort. It updates itself after that. On Windows, SmartScreen may warn the first time:
            the app is signed with a free, self-signed certificate.</p>
          <div class="dls">
            {DOWNLOADS.map((d) => (
              <a class="dl" href={downloadUrl(d.asset)} data-os={d.os} data-first={FIRST[d.os]}>
                <strong>{d.label}</strong><span>{d.detail}</span>
              </a>
            ))}
          </div>
          <p class="first" data-first-out aria-live="polite"><b>First start:</b> <span>{FIRST.windows}</span></p>
          <a class="small" href={RELEASES}>Release notes and checksums</a>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step reveal">
        <span class="num mid">2</span>
        <div class="body with-model">
          <div class="model"><HeadsetModel size="320px" aspect="1 / 1" /></div>
          <h3>Connect the Frame: wirelessly or with a cable</h3>
          <div class="conn" data-conn="url">
            <div class="seg" role="tablist" aria-label="How to connect">
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-conn-btn="url">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 14a4 4 0 0 0 5.6 0l3-3a4 4 0 0 0-5.6-5.6l-1 1M14 10a4 4 0 0 0-5.6 0l-3 3a4 4 0 0 0 5.6 5.6l1-1"/></svg>
                Setup page</button>
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-conn-btn="wifi">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 8.5a15 15 0 0 1 20 0M5 12a10 10 0 0 1 14 0M8.5 15.5a5 5 0 0 1 7 0M12 19h.01"/></svg>
                Wi-Fi</button>
              <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-conn-btn="usb">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v14M8 7l4-4 4 4M7 11v2a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h3M17 9v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-3"/><circle cx="12" cy="19" r="2"/></svg>
                USB cable</button>
            </div>
            <div class="for-url">
              <p>In FramePort click <b>Steam Frame → Start setup</b>. On the Frame open the <b>SteamVR dashboard →
                Desktop</b>, then <b>Konsole</b>, and run the same line on every Frame: it finds FramePort on your network
                (Wi-Fi or a USB cable) and asks you to allow it on the PC.</p>
              <div class="cmd static"><code><span class="prompt">$</span>curl -sL spoopyghosty0.github.io/frameport/s | bash</code>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-small" data-copy-line="curl -sL spoopyghosty0.github.io/frameport/s | bash">Copy</button></div>
              <p class="small-p">No address or code to type. <a href={url('setup/')}>The setup page</a>, with copy-paste from the
                Frame's own browser and every other way.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="for-wifi">Keep the Frame and this computer on the same Wi-Fi, or join the Frame's own hotspot. In
              FramePort click <b>Steam Frame → Show setup command</b>.</p>
            <p class="for-usb">On the Frame turn on Developer Mode (<b>Steam button → Settings → System → Enable Developer
              Mode</b>) and connect its USB-C port to this computer with a data cable. In FramePort click <b>Steam Frame →
              Set up with a USB cable</b>; it finds the Frame on the cable by itself. No router, no firewall question.</p>
            <p class="for-line">On the Frame open the <b>SteamVR dashboard → Desktop</b>, then <b>Konsole</b>, and type the command FramePort
              shows:</p>
            <div class="cmd explain for-line" data-cmd>
              <code><span class="prompt">$</span><span class="tok" tabindex="0" data-tip="Downloads the setup script from FramePort on your computer.">curl</span> <span class="tok" tabindex="0" data-tip="Quietly, and stops on any error instead of running half a script.">-fsS</span> <span class="tok ph" tabindex="0" data-tip="Your computer on the network. Over the cable it is always 10.86.200.234."><span class="for-wifi">&lt;pc-address&gt;</span><span class="for-usb">10.86.200.234</span></span><span class="tok" tabindex="0" data-tip="The port of FramePort's setup server, open only while the setup command is shown.">:8765</span><span class="tok ph" tabindex="0" data-tip="A one-time code: the server answers only this Frame, once.">/&lt;code&gt;</span> <span class="tok" tabindex="0" data-tip="Runs it: SSH key, Developer Mode, Lepton. Read it in bootstrap/bootstrap.sh.">| bash</span></code>
            </div>
            <p class="tip for-line" data-tip-out aria-live="polite">Point at a part of the command to see what it does.</p>
            <p class="small-p">No root, no <code>sudo</code>, no password. <a href={url('docs/frame-setup/')}>What it changes on
              the Frame</a> · <a href={blob('bootstrap/bootstrap.sh')}>The script</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step reveal">
        <span class="num frame">3</span>
        <div class="body">
          <h3>Add games, install</h3>
          <p><b>Add games → Scan a folder</b>, pick a game, <b>Install on Frame</b>. When it's done the game is in your
            Steam library on the Frame.</p>
          <a class="video" href={url('media/frameport-install.mp4')}>
            <video muted loop playsinline preload="none" poster={url('media/frameport-install.jpg')} data-preview={url('media/preview-install.mp4')} width="1280" height="720" aria-hidden="true"></video>
            <span><Glyph name="live" size={18} /> The install tutorial · 80 s</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="makers reveal" id="button">
      <div class="makers-copy">
        <p class="label"><b>For game makers</b></p>
        <h3>An “Install with FramePort” button</h3>
        <p class="muted">Put it on your download page. A click opens FramePort, which asks, downloads and installs your
          build on the visitor's Frame. Without FramePort, the button's page explains how to get it.</p>
        <div class="badge-row"><InstallBadge id="makers" href={url('install/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fexample.com%2Fgames%2Fcool-game-arm64.apk')}
          label="Try it: what a visitor without FramePort sees" /><span class="try">← try it</span></div>
        <a class="small" href={url('docs/install-button/')}>The button, the manifest format and the rules</a>
      </div>
      <div class="snippet">
        <div class="snippet-bar"><span>HTML</span><button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-small" data-copy>Copy</button></div>
        <pre><code data-snippet>{snippet}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  // first start: the steps for the system under the pointer, else this computer's
  const firstOut = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-first-out] span');
  const dls = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.dl[data-first]')];
  const mine = () => dls.find((d) => d.hasAttribute('aria-current')) ?? dls[0];
  const setFirst = (d?: HTMLElement) => { if (firstOut && d) firstOut.textContent = d.dataset.first!; };
  requestAnimationFrame(() => setFirst(mine()));
  dls.forEach((d) => {
    d.addEventListener('pointerenter', () => setFirst(d)); d.addEventListener('focus', () => setFirst(d));
    d.addEventListener('pointerleave', () => setFirst(mine()));
  });
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy-line]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(b.dataset.copyLine!); b.textContent = 'Copied'; } catch { b.textContent = 'Select and copy'; }
    setTimeout(() => { b.textContent = 'Copy'; }, 1600);
  }));
  // setup page, Wi-Fi command or USB cable
  const conn = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-conn]');
  conn?.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-conn-btn]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
    conn.dataset.conn = b.dataset.connBtn!;
    conn.querySelectorAll('[data-conn-btn]').forEach((o) => o.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(o === b)));
  }));
  // the command explains itself, part by part
  const out = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-tip-out]');
  const idle = out?.textContent ?? '';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cmd] .tok').forEach((t) => {
    const on = () => { if (out) { out.textContent = t.dataset.tip!; out.classList.add('on'); } t.classList.add('lit'); };
    const off = () => { if (out) { out.textContent = idle; out.classList.remove('on'); } t.classList.remove('lit'); };
    t.addEventListener('pointerenter', on); t.addEventListener('focus', on);
    t.addEventListener('pointerleave', off); t.addEventListener('blur', off);
  });
  const btn = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy]');
  btn?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    const text = document.querySelector('[data-snippet]')?.textContent ?? '';
    try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text); btn.textContent = 'Copied'; }
    catch { btn.textContent = 'Select and copy'; }
    setTimeout(() => { btn.textContent = 'Copy'; }, 1800);
  });
</script>

<style>
  .steps { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 18px; counter-reset: none; }
  .step { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 76px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 24px; padding: 28px; border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .num { font: 800 64px/0.9 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -0.04em; }
  .num.pc { color: var(--secondary); }
  .num.mid { background: var(--portal); -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; color: transparent; }
  .num.frame { color: var(--accent); }
  .body { display: grid; gap: 14px; align-content: start; min-width: 0; }
  .body h3 { font-size: 22px; }
  .body p { color: var(--text-2); max-width: 70ch; }
  .body b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .small, .small-p { font-size: 14px; }
  .first { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-2); min-height: 3em; }
  .first b { color: var(--text); }
  .conn { display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  .with-model { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 280px; column-gap: 28px; }
  .with-model > :not(.model) { grid-column: 1; }
  .with-model .model { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1 / span 3; align-self: center; }
  .seg { display: inline-flex; justify-self: start; padding: 4px; gap: 4px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--surface-3); }
  .seg button { all: unset; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 8px 16px; border-radius: 999px; cursor: pointer;
    font: 600 14px/1 var(--font-sans); color: var(--text-2); transition: background-color 220ms, color 220ms; }
  .seg button[aria-selected="true"] { color: var(--on-accent); background: var(--accent); }
  .seg button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  [data-conn="wifi"] .for-usb, [data-conn="usb"] .for-wifi, [data-conn="url"] :is(.for-wifi, .for-usb, .for-line),
  :not([data-conn="url"]) > .for-url { display: none; }
  .for-url { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  .cmd.static code { font-size: 14px; }
  .explain code { white-space: nowrap; }
  .tok { border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 2px; cursor: help; transition: background-color 150ms, color 150ms, box-shadow 150ms; }
  .tok:hover, .tok:focus-visible, .tok.lit { outline: none; background: rgba(255, 138, 31, .18); color: var(--text); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 138, 31, .5); }
  .tip { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-2); min-height: 1.6em; transition: color 150ms; }
  .tip.on { color: var(--accent); }
  .small-p code { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text); }
  .dls { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }
  .dl { display: grid; gap: 2px; padding: 10px 16px; min-width: 150px; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); color: var(--text); transition: border-color 220ms, background-color 220ms; }
  .dl span { font: 400 12px/1.4 var(--font-mono); color: var(--text-2); }
  .dl:hover { border-color: var(--secondary-line); background: rgba(58, 168, 255, 0.06); }
  .dl[aria-current] { border-color: var(--accent); background: rgba(255, 138, 31, 0.08); }
  .dl[aria-current] strong::after { content: " · this computer"; font-weight: 400; color: var(--accent); font-size: 13px; }
  .video { position: relative; display: block; max-width: 520px; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--border); box-shadow: var(--shadow-art); text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform 220ms var(--ease-out), box-shadow 220ms var(--ease-out); }
  .video img, .video video { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; object-fit: cover; background: #050608; }
  .video span { position: absolute; left: 12px; bottom: 12px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;
    padding: 6px 12px; border-radius: var(--radius-pill); background: rgba(13, 14, 18, 0.75); color: var(--text);
    font: 600 13px/1 var(--font-sans); }
  .video:hover { transform: translateY(-3px); box-shadow: var(--shadow-art-hover); }

  .makers { margin-top: clamp(48px, 7vw, 80px); display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr); gap: 32px;
    padding: 32px; border-radius: var(--radius-md); border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong); background: var(--portal-glow); }
  .makers-copy { display: grid; gap: 14px; align-content: start; }
  .makers-copy .label { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .makers-copy h3 { font-size: 24px; }
  .badge-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; margin-block: 6px; }
  .try { font: 500 13px/1 var(--font-mono); color: var(--text-2); }
  .snippet { min-width: 0; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    overflow: hidden; align-self: start; }
  .snippet-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 6px 8px 6px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font: 600 11px/1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .12em; color: var(--text-2); }
  .snippet pre { margin: 0; padding: 16px; overflow-x: auto; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text); }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .step { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px; padding: 22px 18px; }
    .num { font-size: 48px; }
    .makers { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: 22px 18px; }
    .with-model { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .with-model .model { grid-column: 1; grid-row: auto; max-width: 240px; justify-self: center; }
  }
</style>
